<br/>
<br/>New for MoP Classic, all previous tier sets have been disabled for level 90 players. This combined with the lack of benefit from equipping either the Protection or Retribution versions of this tier makes equipping four pieces of Tier 14 a simple choice for PvE content.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Holy Paladins Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>In general, Holy Paladin's trinkets for should be centered around mana-regen, particularly prior to full BiS. That said, modern changes in Mists of Pandaria Classic have made Holy Paladin's slightly less mana hungry that is traditional,  and players in strong guilds may find that they quickly grow out of mana concerns and can find room for output trinkets.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>You should typically use one on-use and one passive trinket, or two passive trinkets, but rarely ever two on-use. The various options are listed below in order of relative strength (within their respective category). <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87163/spirits-of-the-sun">
<img alt="Spirits of the Sun" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_29_sunkissedwine.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirits of the Sun</span></a> is far and away the best trinket available in Phase One. As a mana regen proc, there is largely no need to play around it in any particular way and it can simply be equipped and enjoyed.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86805/qin-xis-polarizing-seal">
<img alt="Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal</span></a> seems very similar to the highly valued Spirit proc Trinkets at first glance, merely just reversed; in reality however it is slightly worse as Holy Paladin has few methods to take advantage of Intellect procs, while Spirit procs are always valuable (provided one is not at full mana). Fortunately the long duration and short internal cooldown of this trinket means it should be active very frequently.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is the Healer Darkmoon Deck of the expansion, and as is typical it is quite strong. Like Spirts of the Sun, Relic of Chi-Ji is very simple to use.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81266/price-of-progress">
<img alt="Price of Progress" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Price of Progress</span></a>, while working slightly differently than the Spirit proc trinkets, is functionally the same.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> while only available to Alchemists, Mists of Pandaria's version of this profession Trinket can be very powerful when used to its full potential.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81133/empty-fruit-barrel">
<img alt="Empty Fruit Barrel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cask_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Empty Fruit Barrel</span></a> is largely identical to Qin-xi's Polarizing Seal, but much weaker than the alternative options available.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89080/scroll-of-revered-ancestors">
<img alt="Scroll of Revered Ancestors" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_highborne_scroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scroll of Revered Ancestors</span></a> can be thought of as effectively a mana potion, and should be used on cooldown whenever not at maximum mana. With a cooldown of 60 seconds it will be available very often.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> is the strongest throughput Healing active Trinket available in Phase One, though the fact that it gives Critical Strike unfortunately makes it weaker than the three best passive Trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81264/vial-of-ichorous-blood">
<img alt="Vial of Ichorous Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Ichorous Blood</span></a> is a similar but weaker variant of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89080/scroll-of-revered-ancestors">
<img alt="Scroll of Revered Ancestors" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_highborne_scroll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scroll of Revered Ancestors</span></a> used in the same manner.</div></li></ul>
