<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Holy Paladin</span></h2>With the Mists of Pandaria the new <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=112859/holy-insight">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_spiritualguidence.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Insight</span></a> passive has been introduced, granting a 100% hit chance on <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=20473/holy-shock">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_searinglight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Shock</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=20271/judgment">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_righteousfury.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Judgment</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=2812/denounce">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_purifyingpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Denounce</span></a>, which constitutes the entirety of the Holy Paladin's relevant ability to do damage. There remains some exceedingly minor relevancy to Hit and Expertise due to the occasional need to melee attack for mana via <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=20165/seal-of-insight">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_healingaura.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of Insight</span></a>, but any potential gain here is so infinitesimally small that it nearly does not bear any mentioning at all.  Pieces with these stats can be used if there is absolutely no alternative available, but there is zero reason to ever consider pursuing Hit or Expertise cap on Holy Paladin in Mists of Pandaria, and healer pieces will always outperform any precision gear.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Holy Paladins</span></h2>Gems in Mists of Pandaria give twice as much secondary stats as they do main stat, meaning that there is an ideal option available for each slot color. As with their, gear Holy Paladins should prioritize Intellect, Spirit, and Mastery here; use <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76686/purified-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Purified Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Imperial Amethyst</span></a> in Blue and Red slots and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76645/zen-wild-jade">
<img alt="Zen Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Wild Jade</span></a> in Yellow. <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76694/brilliant-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Primordial Ruby</span></a> can be used if you have out geared any relevant mana-regeneration needs, and will be dependent on playstyle, talent choice, content type, and group ability.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76879/ember-primal-diamond">
