<img alt="Sparkling Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sparkling Tinker's Gear</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_craftsman.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Holy Paladins</span></h2>In a similar fashion to racials an other aspects of character differentiation, in Mists of Pandaria most professions are all relatively close together, though as always gathering professions, (with the debatable exception of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=182/herbalism">
<img alt="Herbalism" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_herbalism.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Herbalism</span></a>), do fall significantly behind. Like Cataclysm, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> are the default choices due to their movement speed boosts.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Holy Paladins</h4>The perennial recommended profession for all classes, Engineering continues to be a powerful profession due to its access to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>. On average <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is equal to the stat gains of other professions, but being an active it allows the user to combine it with other cooldowns to multiply its benefit, (while also running the risk of the opposite happening due to misplay). If this wasn't enough, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77538/specialized-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Specialized Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Specialized Retinal Armor</span></a> is a Epic pre-raid option only available to engineers.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="leatherworking">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_leatherworking.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Leatherworking for Holy Paladins</h4>Leatherworking gives the standard profession boost of 320 Intellect via <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=124552/fur-lining-intellect">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pelt_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Intellect</span></a>. Similar to Engineering its true value lies in access to extra items, in this case the notorious <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=185851/greater-drums-of-speed">
<img alt="Greater Drums of Speed" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_drum_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Greater Drums of Speed</span></a>.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Holy Paladins</h4>Tailoring is an interesting choice for Holy Paladins. While like Leatherworking the gear itself isn't useful, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125481/lightweave-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_thread_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweave Embroidery</span></a> is a powerful proc that like Synapse Springs can be used to great effect with intelligent play. The downside is that the proc is much harder to play around than an on-demand active, and while its activation is predictable it is not preventable, opening up the potential for it to be completely wasted. Furthermore, Tailoring does not have an immediate second benefit as Engineering and Leatherworking do.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Holy Paladins</span></h3>For the most part, crafted items are no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Blacksmith, you can equip anything Blacksmiths craft. While not the best choice for any slot, and likely expensive at the beginning of the expansion, visiting the auction house can mean an easy power boost while waiting for the rest of the Phase One raids to become available. It is worth keep in mind however that, with the exception of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a>, any crafted item will be used for an exceedingly short amount of time, and the alternative options are relatively easy to acquire. If you do have excess gold the following items are worth some consideration and are all strong, particularly before Celestial Dungeons are available:<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87403/chestplate-of-limitless-faith">
<img alt="Chestplate of Limitless Faith" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidpaladin_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chestplate of Limitless Faith</span></a> is a Blacksmithing BoE piece that requires both a raid pattern and raid mats, and is thus likely to be relatively expensive. Considering this is a tier slot most should overlook this option, though it is strong in a vacuum.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87404/gauntlets-of-unbound-devotion">
<img alt="Gauntlets of Unbound Devotion" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_plate_raidpaladin_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of Unbound Devotion</span></a> is another BoE Blacksmithing option in a tier slot, with the same pros and cons as before.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82968/masterwork-lightsteel-shield">
<img alt="Masterwork Lightsteel Shield" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_pandariatradeskill_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Masterwork Lightsteel Shield</span></a> is the last of the Blacksmithing options, but unlike the others does not require any raid content. Shields are quite limited early on in Mists of Pandaria, and this is a perfectly itemized option that should be cheaply available.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is the expansion's Darkmoon Deck for healers,<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79325/crane-deck"> created by gathering cards from Inscription</a>, and is typically both very strong and likely to be very expensive.</div></li></ul>
